From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-input: the multitouch device is a touch screen only (#843)

What: virtio-multitouch no longer takes the UIs' button events and no longer
shows the guest a mouse's buttons: its handler takes multitouch events only,
and of the keys it has BTN_TOUCH alone.

Why: OmacVM attaches it on a Mac with a touch display, for a pinch's two
fingers (omacvm-cocoa-touch.patch), next to the tablet. QEMU sends a button
event to the first handler that takes buttons, and a virtio device's handler
goes to the front when the guest's driver starts it: with the mouse's
buttons on it, clicks went to whichever of the two the guest started last
(to the touch screen: lost). The guest also took it for a mouse as well as
a touch screen (udev: ID_INPUT_MOUSE and ID_INPUT_TOUCHSCREEN; Hyprland
listed it under both), measured in the guest with a uinput copy of the
device: without the buttons it is a touch screen only. Its contacts need no
BTN_TOUCH events (multitouch slots carry them; QEMU's GTK UI sends its
BTN_TOUCH presses to the first button handler, OmacVM's Cocoa UI none).

Upstream: the same change was posted to qemu-devel in December 2025
("hw/input/virtio-input-hid: remove mouse buttons on virtio-multitouch-pci",
for Android guests with a mouse and a multitouch device); not merged.
Test: app/runtime/Tests/touch/test-touch.sh (with the patched sources: the
handler's mask and the keys).
Applies after qemu-cocoa-pinch-zoom.patch.

--- a/hw/input/virtio-input-hid.c
+++ b/hw/input/virtio-input-hid.c
@@ -509,9 +509,15 @@
 
 /* ----------------------------------------------------------------- */
 
+/*
+ * OmacVM (#843): a touch screen only, no mouse's buttons. With them the UI's
+ * button events went to whichever of this device and the tablet the guest
+ * started last (a click lost to the touch screen), and the guest took the
+ * touch screen for a mouse as well.
+ */
 static const QemuInputHandler virtio_multitouch_handler = {
     .name  = VIRTIO_ID_NAME_MULTITOUCH,
-    .mask  = INPUT_EVENT_MASK_BTN | INPUT_EVENT_MASK_MTT,
+    .mask  = INPUT_EVENT_MASK_MTT,
     .event = virtio_input_handle_event,
     .sync  = virtio_input_handle_sync,
 };
@@ -571,11 +577,15 @@
         ABS_MT_POSITION_X,
         ABS_MT_POSITION_Y,
     };
+    /* OmacVM (#843): BTN_TOUCH only (a touch screen's), not a mouse's buttons. */
+    unsigned short keys[] = {
+        BTN_TOUCH,
+    };
 
     vhid->handler = &virtio_multitouch_handler;
     virtio_input_init_config(vinput, virtio_multitouch_config);
-    virtio_input_extend_config(vinput, keymap_button,
-                               ARRAY_SIZE(keymap_button),
+    virtio_input_extend_config(vinput, keys,
+                               ARRAY_SIZE(keys),
                                VIRTIO_INPUT_CFG_EV_BITS, EV_KEY);
     virtio_input_extend_config(vinput, abs_props,
                                ARRAY_SIZE(abs_props),
